Dennom was very excited to find a blindfold on DL2, the
prior ranger never found a blindfold or a towel. Now, of
course, the RNG refused to give up telepathy! Finally got it
much later from Venus during a prayer! 

The first level of the mines was lit so Dennom and Samwise
entered in hopes of scoring some armor and a pick axe. That
worked well, soon the AC dipped from +6 to -9 thanks to +4
hard shoes, a hard hat, a large shield and some dwarven
mithril. That encouraged Dennom enough to try another level
of the mines. With that AC, a brass lantern and a growing
pet it wasn't difficult. It turned out to be a bones level
from a fledgling rogue and didn't yield much of
significance. He did get a cursed sack. Those are handy, the
pets won't move them.

Minetown was the next level, with a co-aligned altar. There
weren't any really special items in any of the shops but
Dennom price IDed everything which later helped to identify
several items without benefit of ?oID, not to mention
helping to know which items were most advantageous to ID.

Next up, Sokoban. Along the way Samwise became a clay golem.
He could easily take down a shopkeeper or priest and kept up
pretty well since he had been zapped with speed monster. The
bad thing, I later discovered, was that he couldn't be
detected with telepathy. Sokoban was uneventful and the
prize was an "oR. Yeah!!

Now Samwise and Dennom trudged back to mine's end where
Dennom was rewarded with a BoH and intrinsic TC from a tengu
not to mention the expected luckstone. Things were looking
up. Back in the main dungeon on DL13 an altar was converted
and a few sacrifices got Magicbane! Dennom had gotten poison
resistance from a centipede corpse at around 8000 turns.
This is when I started feeling this could be the one.

On DL16 Samwise and I danced around a poly trap until he
became a hell hound. This _is_ the top of the line for a "d"
and Sam was a "d" at heart so that seemed fated. Wrong, on
the very next DL poor Samwise was digested by a trapper or
something.

The castle drawbridge was opened with a bugle, which of
course included a typo that alerted all the soldiers to my
presence. After most of the inhabitants of the castle had
come out to play one on one in the maze, Dennom used a
/oStriking and a /oCold to make sure there would be no
accidents here. 

Upon recovery of the /oWish I spent some time considering
going wishless but decided against it. I really mostly just
wanted to ascend a ranger and be done with them. I think
their bow and arrow attacks are inferior and there is too
much work involved in managing their ammunition. That makes
them less fun for me. So I wished up some GDSM and speed
boots (had found ?oCharging) and pressed on.

The quest was uneventful, one zap from a /oSleep and two
whacks from Frost Bane and Scorpius was history. What was
eventful was walking through the maze above the castle on
the way to the quest. Dennom had polyed into a vampire lord
to use the castle moat and was wearing a ring of Sustain
Ability while waiting for the poly to wear off. Dennom met
an unfriendly minotaur just as she returned to human form.
After a couple of round of melee I checked Dennom's HP (AC
-21 and displacement had made me lazy). Yikes! 39/131 HP!

Of course a quick retreat followed by a more enlightened
plan put things aright, but I couldn't imagine a minotaur
could do 92 damage to Dennom that quickly. I theorized that
the =oSA had prevented her from regaining her HP immediately
upon return to human form but a wizmode test suggests that
wasn't the problem.

All of Ghennom was done without any magic mapping or object
detection. Much of it was done without any light (never saw
a magic lamp).

The next interesting moment came in Vlad's tower. No, of
course Vlad didn't cause any trouble, don't be silly. I had
been carrying around a second "oChanging but delayed using
it, thinking I might like to make a few stoning grenades.
After clearing the tower I stopped on the first floor in one
of those closets, locked myself in, put down a couple of
Elbereth's with Magicbane and put on my =oPC and =oP. I'm
sitting there going 9.9.9. when suddenly the door bursts
open!

Well, it was only a giant mummy, but it scared me. So I
killed the M and went to another closet. Outside the door I
engraved three Elbereths and dropped a cursed dart. Inside I
locked the door, did some more Elberething and put the rings
back on. Soon I was a cockatrice. After dropping everything
but the rings I attempted to #sit only to discover my stuff
was in the way! Grrr. And I couldn't move and couldn't open
the door. AND, as I was waiting to regain human form, an L
came along and started summoning stuff. I just knew there
was some combination here that added up to YASD, but not
this time.

Once Dennom returned to human form she put on the "oChange,
enough of this fooling around.

After the VS was marked and the mazes prepared, Dennom
levelported to the mine entrance and zipped down to
Minetown. One last sac (didn't do much sacrificing this
game, got Frost Brand and Magicbane fairly early and didn't
want anything else enough to do the work) to be sure all's
right with the world. Created a lieutenant and killed him.
Now I knew if I sacrificed my own race as a non chaotic, a
hostile demon would be summoned but what did I care, I'd
already killed Juiblex and Yeenoghu.

Well the demon was no problem. It was Venus, the priest and
the altar that were more difficult. I was glad I hadn't
continued to gather and donate gold once 10 points of
protection had been reached. In earlier games I would have
already donated all the gold in the dungeon 3 times (there
was another temple in the main dungeon) and had no way to
get my protection back conveniently. It took a bit of work
but everything but one point of protection was corrected.

After the long walk visiting all the stashes, Dennom
returned to the castle for the final buffing and polishing.
AC was -41 with no undergarment. Alchemy had HP up over 450.
Frost brand was dulled and enchanted until +7 was achieved.
The five +2 daggers were rustproofed, blessed and enchanted
to +7. All the regular arrows Dennom had collected during
the game were stacked up, canceled, blessed, poison coated
and enchanted to +6. There were 902 of them.

The following outlines the significant events from the VotD
to the end of the game. Five c!oGL and about 30 ?oTeleport
were used on the trip out.

