That's only a little over 2500 turns from launch to done.
The mysterious force wasn't nearly as troublesome as usual
and the correct altar was tried first. Only 38 turns were
spent on the Astral Plane.

I spent more real time on DL1 sorting my stuff than I did on
the remainder of the game. I hated to leave any of those
blessed poisoned +6 arrows I had worked so hard to get. I
finally dropped them all and assembled my kit along the
lines of the thread a couple of weeks ago that discussed
minimum and safe requirements for various items. After I had
that worked out I picked up and dropped arrows until I had
exactly as much as I could hold unburdened. Then I picked up
3 times the number I intended to put in the bag from
inventory so that when I put them in the bag I was
unburdened again.

One thing wrong with that plan, I couldn't take anything out
of the bag without becoming burdened, that was inconvenient.

I picked up a crystal ball (becoming burdened) checked to
make sure I had the amulet (you should do that Hawk) and
started to the astral planes. Zapped Rodney with the /oDeath
and then dealt with his pets. Peered into the crystal ball
to locate the portal. It was the longest trip I ever had on
earth. I might have used 12 charges collectively on the 2
/oDig.

I had intended to leave the crystal ball on Earth but when I
saw I was going to be burdened anyway by having the /oDig
out of the bag I decided to used it on Air as well. After
locating the portal, the crystal ball and /oDig were dumped
to get unburdened. That, along with the speed boots made it
much faster but Dennom still got down below 300 HP at one
point.

On Fire, a !oConfusion and a ?oGD did the trick. With the
=oLev still on, Dennom made a beeline over the lava to the
portal. On Water, Dennom used a c?oGD to get in the area and
a /oSDD for the last few steps. Dennom left the bubble with
no grease (never saw any this game) and no oilskin cloak. He
hoped what he had heard about teleporting monsters away if
they grabbed you worked. Turned out that with speed boots
and MC3 he never was grabbed.

On Astral, Dennom started left, I always do, it looks
closer. After fighting the initial arch-lich, Dennom pretty
much didn't fight anything but maybe to swat the occasional
bug that was in his way. /oDeath for Famine, Elbereth or a
quick swat from +2 Magicbane for the bugs and /oTeleport for
almost everything else.

Did you ever notice that when you step in the correct
temple, the monsters start fleeing. I guess if they don't,
there's no need to fight your way over to the altar.

